Each file argument with an unsupported extension (`.txt`), nested path included, gets its own error on stderr, so stdout is empty and outln exits 1.
== args
alpha.txt
nested/beta.txt
== file alpha.txt
const alpha = 1;
== file nested/beta.txt
const beta = 2;
== stdout
== stderr
FILE alpha.txt HAS UNSUPPORTED FILE TYPE
FILE nested/beta.txt HAS UNSUPPORTED FILE TYPE
== exit 1
